Sources:
- Dumusque et al. 2021, HARPS-N solar telescope, first public release 2015-2018 (DACE)
  <https://dace.unige.ch/>
- Trifonov et al. 2020, HARPS RVBank, VizieR J/A+A/636/A74 (HD 10700, tau Ceti)
  <https://vizier.cds.unistra.fr/viz-bin/VizieR?-source=J/A%2BA/636/A74>
- SDO/HMI, hmi.Ic_720s keyword RSUN_OBS, JSOC <http://jsoc.stanford.edu/>
Evidence class (rule 10): check
Where the Earth's radius enters:
- SUN_DAYS, TAU_CETI velocities: rebuilt as RV - BERV: the barycentric correction added back is
  computed from ephemerides, with the Earth's radius
- SDO_RSUN: the apparent radius is computed by the SDO pipeline from the spacecraft-Sun distance, an
  ephemeris
What would vindicate the flat model (rule 5): Doppler residuals at the level of the instrument,
  about 1 m/s, for some height of the flat model's Sun; a zenith star that stays put through the
  year to better than a second of arc.
